# Call-site ledger of path at 0f86209f11199ceaff788c73f96ea5b5ec2318ee.
# Decide every `undecided` line; see macro-benchmark/README.md.
#
# path.md records the judgements. In short: Path subclasses str; the
# package value of the class attribute `module` is os.path (named os.path.*
# on every platform); a module that a client puts there (using_module, or an
# assignment to `module` as the tests do) is a client object (B5), so its
# functions are no callees. A `str` parameter whose role is a path admits a
# Path (the tests and the docstrings pass Paths there); a `str` parameter of
# another role (a mode, an encoding, a hash name, a pattern) admits no
# package value (B3).
default reject path.SpecialResolver.ResolverScope.__getattr__, path.SpecialResolver.__getattr__: the receiver is not a SpecialResolver or a ResolverScope, or normal lookup finds the attribute (the instance attributes path_class, wrapper, paths and scope, which __init__ sets, and the class attributes ResolverScope and get_dir); only a client's attribute load on these objects reaches __getattr__
default reject path.classes.ClassProperty.__get__: the attribute is not `_next_class` or `special`, the only names that a ClassProperty binds (the entries of the `_next_class` loads accept it)
default reject path.classes.multimethod.__get__: the attribute is not `joinpath`, the only name that a multimethod binds, and the package never loads `joinpath`
default reject path.Multi.__iter__: no iteration, `in` test or builtin call in the package iterates a Multi instance; the iterated values are tuples, lists, sets, str values, dicts, generators, filter, map and itertools objects, os.listdir and glob results, re results and a stub (the package returns Multi values to the client, and the only package code that keeps one, Path.__enter__ storing self.cwd() and __exit__ passing it to os.chdir, does not iterate it; padded and compose take any iterable or callable, B3)
default reject path.Path.__enter__, path.Path.__exit__, path.TempDir.__enter__, path.TempDir.__exit__: no with statement in the package is over a Path; the items are contextlib.suppress objects, the file objects that open returns, and DirectoryNotEmpty.translate()

